entries=f'''\n\n## V542 | {now} | Q7 third-root tail-only certificate\n\n**Claim.** The third increasing Q7 two-mode compatibility root has sufficient exterior R>2^(109/2)|epsilon|^(7/2).\n\n**Method.** Use the admitted226 tail-only comparison with a2048-bit Cartesian prefix through140; independently replay at3072 bits using positive-frequency polar recurrence and two full provisional continuations at every resonance. Recompute every compact tail leaf, its integer range, and the exact scalar map.\n\n**Result.** All280 norm and19 tuning comparisons pass. The independent replay checks31,010 products and62,243 Poisson columns. Eight direct responses and two closed Taylor leaves certify |sigma_k|>2^-19 for every k>=20. All42 scalar identities and the rational box pass at q109. The four stages took454.45,636.73,10.54 and9.96seconds.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED and PROVED.** This improves the sufficient exponent from56 to109/2; it does not identify the true boundary. Evidence: research/262_tail_response_prefix/PROOF.md and verification/Q7_admission.json.\n\n## V543 | {now} | Completed root1 reruns and extended root3 comparisons\n\n**Claim.** The six completed Q7/Q8 floating outputs reproduce their checked prefixes and their printed block-fit statistics.\n\n**Method.** Compare the frozen files to the independent directed prefixes through56/64 for root1 and140/96 for root3. Reconstruct exact rational normal equations for every complete-block window.\n\n**Result.** All1,184 norm comparisons,74 tuning comparisons and36 fits pass. Q7 root3 norm-log discrepancies are below1e-10 in both formats. Q8 root3 discrepancies are below1e-7 in binary64 and1e-10 in extended precision. Both root1 reruns complete, with density apparent radii5058.30--5273.56 and77597.86--84823.81 across the stated windows. Last complete blocks are294/296. Arithmetic took0.20953seconds.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED for finite reproducibility; OPEN for asymptotic constants.** Evidence: research/263_floating_period_growth_audit/EXTENDED_TABLE.md and verification/extended_admission.json.\n\n## V544 | {now} | Exact limiting sin9 response\n\n**Claim.** For delta4/7 and unit f1=sin(9theta), the limiting response is82651586141768218752124086777/415161675019179052311193843662848000.\n\n**Method.** Independently derive the high-carrier t=0 recurrence, evaluate it with exact rational Laurent dictionaries, compare304 exact prefix coefficients, and check the result against a fresh1536-bit compact response and the stored1024-bit point.\n\n**Result.** All checks pass;4,360 rational products give1.9908289014863907558e-7. It is strictly above9e-8. Arithmetic took0.13818seconds.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED exact limit; REFUTED if the earlier finite fit range[5e-9,9e-8] is interpreted as a limit enclosure.** No claim about asymptotic growth of H follows from this limit alone. Evidence: research/265_single_nine_exact_limit/PROOF.md and verification/admission.json.\n'''
